tively visible geometry and site markers);\n  - `intrinsic`: 3x3 pinhole K (pixel u right, v down; principal point at the image centre);\n  - `camera_to_world`: 4x4 pose of the OpenCV optical frame (x right, y down, z forward) in the\n    MuJoCo world frame (metres, +Z up);\n  - `robot`: `joint_names`, `joint_positions` (7 arm joints in rad, 2 finger slides in m),\n    `joint_velocities`, `hand_position` (world m), `hand_quaternion_wxyz`, `tcp_position`\n    (midpoint between the finger pads), `gripper_opening` (finger separation normalised to 0..1),\n    `mocap_target_position` (the hand controller's current XYZ target).\n  Cameras: `topview`, `corner`, `corner2`, `corner3`, `corner4` are fixed; `behindGripper` and\n  `gripperPOV` move with the hand. Images are raw camera renders: several fixed cameras are\n  mounted rolled, so an image can appear upside down; the calibration describes the pixel\n  geometry exactly.\n- `robot.step(action)`: ONE control `[dx, dy, dz, grip]`, four finite numbers in [-1, 1]. The\n  hand controller target moves by 0.01 m per unit (world frame, clipped to the mocap bounds in\n  spec) and the hand follows; the wrist is fixed. grip > 0 closes, < 0 opens. Each control runs\n  5 physics steps of 2.5 ms (80 Hz). Requests are validated strictly and rejected (HTTP 400),\n  never\n\n… 673 characters not shown …\n\nally, and a saved image is only as recent as the last observe() of that camera.\n\nOne continuous episode: at most 500 controls and 3600 seconds from activation. Observing,\nthinking, coding and controlling all consume this wall budget. When status().ended is true,\nstop sending controls and finish your response immediately. Protected evidence is sealed\nautomatically after you stop; your own trajectory or reward files are not used for scoring.\n/app\ntotal 20\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root root 4096 Sep 28 17:31 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root root 4096 Sep 28 22:24 ..\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 root root 2917 Sep 28 17:31 API.md\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 root root 1658 Sep 28 17:18 limited_client.py\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 root root 4096 Sep 28 17:31 output\n","n":3173,"te":2.3},{"k":"run","t":7.3,"tool":"exec","cmd":"python - <<'PY'\nimport limited_client as robot\nprint('SPEC', robot.spec())\nprint('STATUS', robot.status())\no=robot.observe('corner')\nprint('ROBOT', o['robot'])\nprint('K', o['intrinsic'])\nprint('C2W', o['camera_to_world'])\nPY","status":"ok","wall":1.0,"out":"SPEC {'action_lower': [-1.0, -1.0, -1.0, -1.0], 'action_scale_m': 0.01, 'action_semantics': '[dx, dy, dz, grip]: mocap XYZ displacement = clip(a,-1,1)*0.01 m per control (world frame, target clipped to mocap bounds); grip +1 closes, -1 opens', 'action_shape': [4], 'action_upper': [1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0], 'agent_seconds': 3600.0, 'cameras': ['topview', 'corner', 'corner2', 'corner3', 'corner4', 'behindGripper', 'gripperPOV'], 'control_hz': 80.0, 'height': 480, 'max_actions': 500, 'mocap_lower': [-0.5, 0.4, 0.05], 'mocap_upper': [0.5, 1.0, 0.5], 'physics_steps_per_control': 5, 'physics_timestep': 0.0025, 'protocol': 'metaworldplus-limited-v1', 'width': 480, 'world_frame': 'MuJoCo world, metres, +Z up'}\nSTATUS {'actions': 0, 'active': True, 'ended': False, 'max_actions': 500, 'physics_steps': 0, 'remaining_seconds': 3588.01902759308}\nROBOT {'gripper_opening': 1.0, 'hand_position': [0.004584200424389321, 0.6013881136259894, 0.19514345491770432], 'hand_quaternion_wxyz': [0.7046302959589302, -0.01947243430449178, 0.7090218623566146, 0.020123842064686235], 'joint_names': ['right_j0', 'right_j1', 'right_j2', 'right_j3', 'right_j4', 'right_j5', 'right_j6', 'r_close', 'l_close'], 'joint_positions': [1.8892881812939124, -0.5757689061948442, -0.9766593499473483, 1.641991493813296, 0.9428596255713374, 1.043696239637583, 2.2928333115361488, -0.00017190619515364345, 0.0001717454224666177], 'joint_velocities': [0.2610021407549013, 0.42891258658155484, -0.4857704976975179, 0.24403763935382766, 0.8291097873010733, 0.09876226777705563, 1.5894717647954915, 5.842799054354187e-07, 5.910160138762781